WEBVTT

00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:14,260
Negolace blood tests are advertised as a way to track cancer.

00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:19,660
Is this test something you could use to track cancer

00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:21,380
or reoccurrence?

00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:26,380
One of the pros and cons of relase testing,

00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:29,380
some clinics use it, but also read research

00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:34,140
that can't be reproduced any thoughts on this.

00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:38,580
Well, there's pros and cons to every test.

00:00:38,580 --> 00:00:42,900
So there's different negolace tests that are out there.

00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:47,900
There's the reds negolace test that you could run

00:00:48,580 --> 00:00:51,840
with different clinics and that is sent over

00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:56,500
to Europe to run it.

00:00:56,500 --> 00:01:01,500
None, there are any negolace tests done in the United States.

00:01:02,420 --> 00:01:05,620
So that is sent over to Europe for that test.

00:01:05,620 --> 00:01:07,860
We have never, I don't know, not about it

00:01:07,860 --> 00:01:09,820
because I don't run that test.

00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:13,860
I, when we were looking into it,

00:01:13,860 --> 00:01:17,540
I saw too many inconsistency, so we didn't,

00:01:19,060 --> 00:01:20,940
we just didn't, I just didn't get into it.

00:01:20,940 --> 00:01:24,100
I just didn't feel good about it for many reasons.

00:01:24,100 --> 00:01:25,780
I can't remember all of them.

00:01:27,220 --> 00:01:32,220
There was a person that I know well that uses it

00:01:33,060 --> 00:01:37,980
another practitioner, and she really thinks the best of it,

00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:40,780
but she is not a licensed in any way.

00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:45,220
So she has the no ability to run any other blood work.

00:01:45,220 --> 00:01:47,780
So that was kind of her go-to thing.

00:01:47,780 --> 00:01:52,020
I don't think it is, but I don't think it's very accurate.

00:01:52,020 --> 00:01:55,980
Then there's that test that you can send over to vanilla.

00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:59,660
That's a different test similar to the negolace test,

00:02:00,660 --> 00:02:04,820
but then there in COVID, that became extinct

00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:07,420
because they weren't accepting any more new tests

00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:10,420
because they were inundated with testing.

00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:11,980
Now I don't know.

00:02:11,980 --> 00:02:14,260
Somebody asked a question about that test

00:02:15,780 --> 00:02:17,660
a month or so ago, and they were gonna check

00:02:17,660 --> 00:02:20,620
and see if they're accepting any new tests.

00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:23,820
Now I do think that test, though it seemed even more

00:02:23,820 --> 00:02:28,300
hokey-poky was actually more accurate.

00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:33,940
And that was simply by a making that assumption

00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:36,980
based upon experience, not based upon any research,

00:02:36,980 --> 00:02:39,540
because I don't think there's any research on that test.

00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:41,100
That's a urine test.

00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:47,340
I don't know if that is up and running.

00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:52,260
Again, you do that test in your home.

00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:57,260
That's the Navarro HCG test, but I don't know if that

00:02:57,940 --> 00:02:59,660
what is up and running again.

00:02:59,660 --> 00:03:04,660
Now that would give you a reading of zero to a hundred,

00:03:05,100 --> 00:03:07,860
anything over 50 is positive for cancer.

00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:10,460
It doesn't tell you what type of cancer.

00:03:10,460 --> 00:03:14,420
And it's kind of like a tumor marker test.

00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:21,860
And it's just every years throughout all the 25 years

00:03:21,860 --> 00:03:24,300
and dealing with cancer patients,

00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:29,300
that test was like correct everybody that did it.

00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:34,780
So I was impressed with that test.

00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:40,420
And when people were getting better via their symptoms,

00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:44,540
via evidence on CT scans and PET scans,

00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:46,500
and they would run that Navarro test,

00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,260
the number would come down.

00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:50,540
And you didn't give any data unto yourself.

00:03:50,540 --> 00:03:54,060
So there wasn't any bias or anything.

00:03:54,060 --> 00:03:59,060
So it was just it ran perfectly with other testing.

00:04:00,660 --> 00:04:02,940
So I was very impressed with that test.

00:04:02,940 --> 00:04:06,420
The negative of it was that you had to send it over

00:04:06,420 --> 00:04:08,860
to the Philippines to get red.

00:04:10,100 --> 00:04:13,380
And it took like two to two to four weeks

00:04:13,380 --> 00:04:14,540
to get your results back.

00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:16,460
The positive was so inexpensive.

00:04:16,460 --> 00:04:18,340
I think it was like 55 bucks.

00:04:19,460 --> 00:04:20,740
I don't know what it is now.

00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:23,460
Again, I don't know if it's up and running again.

00:04:24,620 --> 00:04:29,620
So somebody wants to check into the Navarro test.

00:04:31,140 --> 00:04:34,660
The Nagolace test, again, I'm not against them

00:04:34,660 --> 00:04:36,780
and it can be another marker.

00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:42,340
But like any test you measure it on a graph,

00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:47,340
but you measure it from over time.

00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:49,860
And you can see the changes over time,

00:04:49,860 --> 00:04:51,460
but it may be accurate.

00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:54,900
I just we haven't run enough of them to really dull.

00:04:54,900 --> 00:04:57,260
And I haven't had enough people do it

00:04:57,260 --> 00:04:59,700
to really make a proper assessment

00:04:59,700 --> 00:05:01,980
whether I think it was good or not.

